-# Walkthrough - Project Cleanup and Documentation Update
+# Walkthrough - Technical Refactoring and Quality Update
+
+I have performed a significant technical refactoring of the project to improve its architecture, memory management, and compatibility.
 
-I have successfully cleaned up the project by resolving major errors, warnings, and inconsistencies. I have also updated the documentation to reflect the actual project state.
+## Core Architectural Changes
 
-## Changes Made
+### 1. Extracted `ScreenCaptureManager`
+- **New Component:** Created [ScreenCaptureManager.kt](file:///C:/Users/eduardo.asousa/Projetos/Pessoal/MangaLens/app/src/main/java/com/example/service/ScreenCaptureManager.kt) to handle all MediaProjection and ImageReader logic.
+- **Benefits:** Decouples screen acquisition from the foreground service lifecycle, making the code more testable and easier to read.
+- **Memory Safety:** Implemented safe atomic bitmap swapping and explicit recycling of intermediate bitmaps to prevent memory leaks during rapid screen updates.
 
-### Documentation & Legal
-- **[README.md](file:///C:/Users/eduardo.asousa/Projetos/Pessoal/MangaLens/README.md):**
-    - Updated Kotlin version to **2.2.10**.
-    - Updated supported Android version to **7.0+ (API 24)** to match `minSdk`.
-    - Corrected APK filenames to `app-debug.apk` and `app-release.apk`.
-    - Added Windows-specific setup instructions for `.env` creation.
-    - Improved troubleshooting tips for PowerShell.
-- **[LICENSE](file:///C:/Users/eduardo.asousa/Projetos/Pessoal/MangaLens/LICENSE):** Added the missing MIT License file.
+### 2. Refactored `MangaOverlayService`
+- **Modularity:** Updated [MangaOverlayService.kt](file:///C:/Users/eduardo.asousa/Projetos/Pessoal/MangaLens/app/src/main/java/com/example/service/MangaOverlayService.kt) to delegate screen capture to the new manager.
+- **Non-blocking Operations:** Replaced all occurrences of `Thread.sleep` with coroutine-friendly `delay` to prevent UI thread stuttering.
+- **Robust UI State:** Improved the `WindowManager` logic to be more resilient when adding/removing overlays.
 
-### Code Quality & Warning Fixes
-- **General Improvements:**
-    - Replaced deprecated `Divider` with `HorizontalDivider`.
-    - Used `String.toUri()` and `String.toColorInt()` KTX extensions.
-    - Simplified `Build.VERSION.SDK_INT` checks since `minSdk` is 24.
-    - Cleaned up unused imports and parameters across all major files.
-    - Used `Icons.AutoMirrored.Filled.MenuBook` for better localization support.
-- **[MangaReaderViewModel.kt](file:///C:/Users/eduardo.asousa/Projetos/Pessoal/MangaLens/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/reader/MangaReaderViewModel.kt):**
-    - Removed unused functions: `selectChapter`, `selectPanel`, `onUserScrolled`, `toggleHistoryVisibility`, `closeHistory`, and `clearHistory`.
-    - Simplified `triggerTranslation` signature.
+### 3. API Compatibility (Android 7.0+)
+- **Guarded Features:** Re-added proper `Build.VERSION.SDK_INT` checks for API 26 features like `TYPE_APPLICATION_OVERLAY` and `NotificationChannel`.
+- **Backward Compatibility:** Ensured the app falls back to `TYPE_PHONE` for older devices instead of crashing.
 
-### Build Configuration
-- **[app/build.gradle.kts](file:///C:/Users/eduardo.asousa/Projetos/Pessoal/MangaLens/app/build.gradle.kts):**
-    - Fixed string template warning for `$rootDir`.
-    - Removed duplicate dependency declarations (Compose BOM, JUnit, etc.).
+### 4. Robust AI Integration
+- **Improved Parsing:** Updated `GeminiVisualTranslator.kt` with more resilient JSON parsing. It now handles various JSON structures that the Gemini API might return (different array keys, nested objects, and markdown formatting).
+- **Graceful Failures:** Better error propagation from the AI client to the UI.
+
+## Build and Code Quality
+- **Badge Accuracy:** Updated `README.md` badges to reflect **Kotlin 2.2.10** and **Android 7.0+**.
+- **Modern Standards:** Replaced deprecated UI components and optimized string templates.
 
 ## Verification Results
-- All files passed basic semantic analysis (`analyze_file`) with zero errors.
-- The `features` branch is up to date with these changes.
